50: Here lies Tamaio. General, warrior, friend. May his soul rest in death.
51: Here lies Tyrio. Prince and son. May his soul rest in death.

52: Malcolm: What happened here?
53: Malcolm: Ruins everywhere...
54: Malcolm: Dyron... Is that you? What happened?
55: [$FFB1B9]Dyron[$ffffff]: I only had him... I know I was harsh, but... it was because I wanted him to have a good life. And now I've buried him.
56: Malcolm: I'm sorry.
57: [$FFB1B9]Dyron[$ffffff]: My kingdom, my son... All is lost.
58: Malcolm: Not only Hanrain was attacked. Valtaria as well. 
59:[$FFB1B9]Dyron[$ffffff]: Whoever did this will pay for everything.
60:Malcolm: Uh, what are you going to do?
61:[$FFB1B9]Dyron[$ffffff]: Find him and kill him!
62:Malcolm: :5_00139But he has your weapons. You can't defeat him without special weapons.
63:[$FFB1B9]Dyron[$ffffff]: So let's hide. Preferably to another world.
64:Malcolm: Exactly, another world. This armor was created by General X. Just like the last one was destroyed after the Orion War. Go back there and ask for another one.
65:[$FFB1B9]Dyron[$ffffff]: And should I tell him I lost one of his greatest creations?
66:Malcolm: Well, that's out of the question. Forget what I said.:5_00139
67:[$FFB1B9]Dyron[$ffffff]: Akrium. The icy desert terrifies everyone. They'll never find us there.
68:Malcolm: Okay, enough of this. Get a grip!:5_00146 This isn't the Dyron I know. The one I know is resolute, doesn't give up, is able to believe in things that don't exist, and has a plan even in the worst situations.
69:Malcolm: He's the greatest warrior on KamStar, a hero on Earth, and the vanquisher of Orion's army.
70:[$FFB1B9]Dyron[$ffffff]: I once had something to live for.
71:Malcolm: Yes, you lost your son, but you can live for the entire world and defend it. I know the odds are slim, but you've already done something no one believed in.
72:[$FFB1B9]Dyron[$ffffff]: You're right. I can't just give up like that. I have to get my revenge first.
73:Malcolm: That's not the path I'm thinking of, but as long as you're willing to act, I'm fine with it.
74:[$FFB1B9]Dyron[$ffffff]: Okay then. First, tell me briefly how bad it is.
75:Malcolm: Well, very bad. Kregor seems to be ruling Valtaria again, the "Guest" with the axes has disappeared. Ratling is defending himself in the garrison, Ethyroa is in Andaro, I don't know anything about Citland, and Drein is waiting for me to return. And then there's the Grand Inquisition, which answers to Kregor.
76:[$FFB1B9]Dyron[$ffffff]: The Grand Inquisition... Is that all? I thought it was worse. So I have a plan.
77:[$FFB1B9]Dyron[$ffffff]: Let the other kingdoms gather their troops. Drein is with us, he knows secret passages, so we'll attack Kregor unexpectedly. That should distract "The Guest" a bit.
78:Malcolm: Yeah... Cool... And what about "The Guest" with the axes?
79:[$FFB1B9]Dyron[$ffffff]: I didn't forget about him, I left him for last. For last... because I don't know how I'll defeat him yet. But I know who I'll ask for advice: a fortune teller.
80:[$FFB1B9]Dyron[$ffffff]: But that murderer might attack you in Valtaria. This army won't be enough. I know. You'll go to Citland. We'll need Alan's support. 
81:Malcolm: Oh no, not his :5_00142. He's terribly egocentric.
82:[$FFB1B9]Dyron[$ffffff]: That's why you have to meet him. You'll get along like friends. Come with me, I'll transport you to Drein with the ring portal. It'll be faster that way.
83:Malcolm: Not with that demon's creation. Teleportation makes me feel sick.
84:[$FFB1B9]Dyron[$ffffff]: It was created by an architect, not a demon...